{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>This do: take you censers.</b> Moses said: You say that I substituted the Levites in place of the firstborn in order to give greatness to Aaron my brother and to his sons, and that I made the Levites subservient to Aaron, and that I did all this from my own heart and it was not from HaShem — if so, 'this do': bring, you yourselves, the incense offering, which carries the punishment of death by the hand of Heaven for strangers, concerning which the Torah said, ״והזר הקרב יומת״, and if you are delivered from the punishment then I will concede to your words, that the Holy One, blessed be He, does not distinguish between tribe and tribe and does not differentiate between man and man. And this is what they expounded by way of parable: 'a deadly poison was placed within it' — the intention is a counsel by which they would be punished with the death penalty; for if we were to interpret 'deadly poison' literally, it would give an opening to the wicked to say that the punishment did not come from Heaven." "<b>And know</b> that for every occurrence of קטרת in this parashah, Onkelos did not translate it as קטרת בוסמין (incense of spices) according to his custom, but rather קטרת in its plain sense. And it appears that his opinion is that they did not burn actual incense that is קדש (a holy offering), but rather frankincense and the like, as a test; and so he translated in the case of the sons of Aaron. And perhaps he did so because he did not wish to add spices to it but rather only when it is made according to the command of the Torah in its ingredients. But the opinion of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, is that it was incense of קדש, and that is the correct view. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:57.971619742Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}